Convert a motor file between .eng and .rse, write a catalog motor as either, or convert a design between .ork, .hpr and .hprz

Usage: hpr convert [OPTIONS] <INPUT> <OUTPUT>

Arguments:
  <INPUT>
          What to read: a motor file (.eng or .rse), a catalog motor's name, such as H170M, or a design (.ork, .hpr or .hprz)

  <OUTPUT>
          The file to write, by its extension: .eng or .rse for motors, .ork, .hpr or .hprz for a design; it is replaced if it exists

Options:
      --attach <FILE>
          A file to carry in a .hprz beside the design, under its file name; give it once for each

      --json
          Print one JSON document on standard output instead of text; errors too

      --color <WHEN>
          When to use color. Auto colors what goes to a terminal and heeds NO_COLOR, FORCE_COLOR and CLICOLOR_FORCE. JSON output never has color
          
          [default: auto]
          [possible values: auto, always, never]

      --delays <LIST>
          The delays to write in a .eng file's header when the .rse motor gives none, such as 6-10-14, or P for plugged

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version

Examples:
  Write a catalog motor's thrust curve as a .eng file:
      hpr convert H170M H170M.eng
  Turn an OpenRocket design into an HPR design:
      hpr convert my-rocket.ork my-rocket.hpr

Guide: https://hpr.fusionspace.co/cli.html#hpr-convert
